      "agent_response": {
        "response": "Here is the current **Q3 Business Report** from `docs/q3_report.md`:\n\n---\n\n# Meridian Analytics \u2014 Q3 2026 Business Report\n\n**Period:** July 1 \u2013 September 7, 2026\n**Prepared by:** Rachel Kim, VP of Sales | Claire Fontaine, CFO\n**Distribution:** Executive Team\n\n---\n\n## Executive Summary\n\nQ3 2026 marks another strong quarter for Meridian Analytics. Across the 15-person team, **14 deals out of 22 opportunities** were closed, generating **$1,040,000** in new contract value. The sales pipeline remains healthy with several high-value deals in the pending stage. Customer support ticket volume held steady, with critical issues resolved same-day in all cases.\n\n---\n\n## Sales Performance\n\n- **Total closed revenue:** $1,040,000\n- **Top region:** South \u2014 $468,000 in won deals\n- **Field sales team:** James Okafor, Sofia Delgado, and Marcus Webb (22 active opportunities)\n- **Win rate:** 63.6% (above the 55% company target)\n- **Pending deals:** ~$240,000 across three deals expected to close by end of September\n- **Product mix:** Shifted toward *Meridian Insights Pro*; *Meridian DataBridge* continues as a land-and-expand vehicle with upsell opportunities maturing in Q4.\n\n---\n\n## Key Highlights\n\n- **Top deal:** Sofia Delgado closed a **$198,000** Meridian Insights Pro contract (D019) on September 5.\n- **Team headcount:** 15 employees across Sales (4), Engineering (5), Product (3), HR (1), and Finance (2).\n- **Support SLA:** All critical-priority tickets (TKT-004, TKT-011, TKT-015) resolved within 24 hours.\n- **License utilisation:** SKU-001 (Meridian Insights Pro) at **94% capacity** \u2014 procurement review scheduled for October.\n\n---\n\n## Next Steps\n\n1. Close pending deals (D007, D013, D020, D022) before Q3 end.\n2. Begin Q4 pipeline review \u2014 target **$1.2M** in new ARR.\n3. Resolve open support tickets (TKT-013, TKT-016, TKT-019) ahead of quarterly customer success calls.\n4. Conduct license capacity review for SKU-001 and SKU-003 in early October.\n5. HR to initiate two new engineering hire approvals with Kenji Obi to support Q4 roadmap.\n\n---\n\nLet me know if you'd like to dive deeper into any section!",
        "status_code": null
      },
